@id lane_margery
# DRAFT
# Margery hurrying home through the lane at dusk, nights 1 to 6: a line or two of gossip a night, and she's gone.
# Her own flags: lane_margery_<night> (talked to her tonight).
== start
-> start_known [if talked_n0_margery]
-> start_new

== start_known
(Margery, her basket on her arm, walking fast.)
-> tonight

== start_new
(A woman with a covered basket on her arm, walking fast.)
Margery {warm}: Margery, brother, from by Saint Andrew's. I can't stop.
-> tonight

== again
-> back [if night=1] [if lane_margery_1]
-> back [if night=2] [if lane_margery_2]
-> back [if night=3] [if lane_margery_3]
-> back [if night=4] [if lane_margery_4]
-> back [if night=5] [if lane_margery_5]
-> back [if night=6] [if lane_margery_6]
-> hello

== hello
(Margery, her basket on her arm, hurrying past.)
-> tonight

== back
Margery {amused}: Brother, I've told you all I know, and more!
-> end

== tonight
-> n1 [if night=1]
-> n2 [if night=2]
-> n3 [if night=3]
-> n4 [if night=4]
-> n5 [if night=5]
-> n6 [if night=6]

# Night 1
== n1 [set lane_margery_1]
Margery {amused}: You're still with us, then, brother. The lane's been wondering.
-> n1_ask

== n1_ask
* Wondering what? -> n1_what

== n1_what
Margery {amused}: How long you'd last. Oh, don't look at me like that. I'm late.
-> end

# Night 2
== n2 [set lane_margery_2]
-> n2_pond [if died_merchant]
-> n2_rain

== n2_pond
Margery {afraid}: A man in your fishpond! Drowned drunk, your infirmarian says.
Margery {angry}: Drunk! He went past my door as sober as a bishop.
-> n2_ask

== n2_rain
Margery {weary}: Rain again. I'll be soaked through by the corner, and the long way round to go.
-> n2_ask

== n2_ask
* Go carefully. -> n2_care

== n2_care
Margery {amused}: Carefully, in these pattens, in this mud? Pray for me, brother.
-> end

# Night 3
== n3 [set lane_margery_3]
-> n3_tower [if died_warner]
-> n3_plain

== n3_tower
Margery {afraid, swallow}: Hanged in his own bell tower, a holy brother! Your abbot says the devil did it.
Margery {grave}: Devil or rope, he's dead all the same.
-> n3_more

== n3_plain
Margery {wary}: I'm not stopping, brother. Not this week.
-> n3_more

== n3_more
-> n3_jankin [if died_jankin]
-> n3_ask

== n3_jankin
Margery {sad}: And poor Jankin. He owed me tuppence. I'd forgive it twice over to have him back.
-> n3_ask

== n3_ask
* Go safely. -> n3_safe

== n3_safe
Margery {afraid}: Safely! There's no safely, brother. There's quickly.
-> end

# Night 4
== n4 [set lane_margery_4]
Margery {wary}: Your abbot has you all fasting, they say. Fasting against the devil.
Margery {grave}: My gran fasted every Friday of her life, and the devil took her husband anyway.
-> n4_ask

== n4_ask
* Good night, Margery. -> n4_night

== n4_night
Margery {weary}: Good night! I'll settle for a night, brother. Never mind good.
-> end

# Night 5
== n5 [set lane_margery_5]
-> n5_mab [if n4_mab=admitted]
-> n5_more

== n5_mab
Margery {afraid}: You let the leper in! Inside your walls! The whole lane's talking of it.
Margery {warm, glance}: Well. I'd not leave a dog out in that fog either. Don't tell anyone I said so.
-> n5_more

== n5_more
-> n5_edwin [if died_edwin]
-> n5_plain

== n5_edwin
Margery {sad}: That poor young brother. They say he was laid among the bones as if somebody put him to bed.
-> n5_ask

== n5_plain
Margery {afraid}: And I'm not stopping. Not with the light going.
-> n5_ask

== n5_ask
* [if died_edwin] Who says so? -> n5_who
* [if not died_edwin] Go home, Margery. -> n5_home

== n5_who
Margery {grave}: Everybody. Nobody knows who said it first. That's how you know it's true.
-> end

== n5_home
Margery {afraid}: I'm going! What do you think I'm doing?
-> end

# Night 6
== n6 [set lane_margery_6]
Margery {afraid}: Snow! Every step I take, written down for anyone to follow.
(She looks back over her shoulder at her own footprints.)
Margery {pleading}: God keep you tonight, brother. I mean it.
-> n6_ask

== n6_ask
* And you, Margery. [trust margery 5] -> n6_you

== n6_you
Margery {sad}: Me? I'll be under three blankets with the door barred. You're the one who'll be out in it.
-> end

== leave
Margery {warm}: God keep you!
